{
  "about": "A function URL as FF answers it: the table the backend's L1 (url-event.spec.ts, url-response.spec.ts, url-cors.spec.ts and function-url.gateway.spec.ts) and ff local's front door read for their tests, so that both answer alike. `events`: a request, the base `request` with the case's fields in its place (`headers` as sent, in order; `body` as UTF-8 text, or `bodyBase64` for bytes; `withoutHeaders`, the credentials that let the caller in; `caller`, who signed), and its event: the whole `event`, or what it `has`, each part compared whole by its path, and what it `lacks`. `answers`: a function's return value, `output`, and its answer (`status`, `headers` in order, `body` as text or `bodyBase64`) or why it can't be one, `refused`. `cors`: a URL's CORS, `configuration` unless a case gives its own `cors`, each case one question (`ask`) and its answer (`is`). `gateway`: a request to a URL (its `cors` or none; its method, path, headers and body), what the call did (`ran`: the function's `output`, else `{\"statusCode\": 200, \"body\": \"ok\"}`, or its `error`, the function's own unless its `kind` is `throttled`), and the answer as sent: its status, the `headers` it names, in lower case, none whose name starts with `noHeadersStartingWith`'s, its body; whether the function was `called`, or what its event `has`; and what the log `says`.",
  "request": {
    "method": "POST",
    "target": "/my/path?parameter1=value1&parameter1=value2&parameter2=value",
    "headers": [["header1", "value1"], ["header2", "value1"], ["header2", "value2"], ["Cookie", "cookie1; cookie2"], ["User-Agent", "agent"], ["Content-Type", "text/plain"]],
    "body": "Hello from client!",
    "sourceIp": "123.123.123.123",
    "protocol": "HTTP/1.1",
    "domainName": "0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv.fn.example.tn",
    "domainPrefix": "0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv",
    "urlId": "0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv",
    "requestId": "e1506fd5-9e7b-434f-bd42-4f8fa224b599",
    "time": "2020-03-12T19:03:58.390Z",
    "accountId": "anonymous"
  },
  "events": {
    "awsExample": [
      {
        "title": "AWS's own example (its documentation, \"Request payload format\")",
        "request": {},
        "event": {
